@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Local terminal session reset callback
+
+This local patch adds an opt-in callback for terminal integrations that need to discard a
+conversation label immediately after `/clear`, including when the TUI uses a shared daemon.
+It does not change the app-server hook protocol.
+
+Set `CODEX_TUI_SESSION_CLEAR_COMMAND` in the launching shell to the **absolute path of a trusted
+executable**. No shell is used and the value cannot contain arguments. The callback inherits
+the TUI's environment and receives one JSON object on standard input:
+
+```json
+{"version":1,"event":"clear","session_id":"<new thread UUID>"}
+```
+
+The TUI waits for the callback after a successful explicit clear and attachment to the new
+thread, before processing the next input. This also covers “clear and implement the plan.”
+Failed thread replacement, `/compact`, automatic compaction, `/new`, and simple screen
+redraws do not invoke it. The callback does not modify the parent assignment or the old thread.
+
+The executable must be selected by the user or their launcher, outside project configuration.
+An unset variable disables the callback. An invalid path, execution failure, nonzero exit,
+or ten-second timeout produces a visible error without undoing the new conversation.
+Callback stdout/stderr are not rendered in the terminal; integrations should keep diagnostics
+in their own local log if necessary. The callback must finish promptly and must not leave
+background work running. It must verify the target pane before changing terminal metadata.
+
+Only the TUI needs this patch. The existing daemon can continue running. Existing TUI
+processes must be relaunched to use a newly built client; installing the binary does not
+change their code or environment.
